  "worked_solution": "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\u2308x\u2309$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\u2308x\u2309=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\u2308-\\frac{3}{2}\u2309=\u2308-1.5\u2309=-1.\n$$",
